# Ratbot 960 camera + belief-controller test handoff

Recovered from the July 21, 2026 Ratbot history, git commits, README, and Jetson shell history.

## What changed

- Camera capture became configurable instead of being fixed at 640×480 (`7f0cf90`, **Support configurable camera frame size**).
- The live CSI stereo configuration was promoted to **960×720** in `config.yaml`; YOLO `imgsz` was also set to `960` (`a986a7c`, **Promote 960 world tracking config**).
- High-resolution stereo calibration capture was fixed so requested dimensions are preserved (`e991c62`).
- A new 960×720 calibration was captured and committed at `tools/vision/calibration/output_960/stereo_calibration.npz` (`9067fb8`). Its recorded values were stereo RMS `0.810px`, solved baseline `41.64mm`, and physical/effective baseline override `52.5mm`.
- `run.sh rt200` was updated to use that 960 calibration, baseline `52.5`, the TensorRT rat model, CUDA device `0`, and 20 FPS inference by default.
- At the time of the final test, logs confirmed **960×720 CSI stereo**, `cuda:0`, and roughly 18–20 inference FPS after warmup.

