## Run the angular belief controller

World-frame tracking is now enabled by default. Add `--disable-world-tracking` to A/B test the older angular belief controller with the same 960 camera, stereo calibration, model, and servos:

```bash
cd ~/rat-inference
docker stop rat-inference 2>/dev/null || true
./run.sh rt200 --disable-world-tracking
docker logs -f rat-inference
```

The fully explicit non-Docker equivalent recorded in the README was:

```bash
uv run --extra jetson python rt_200.py \
  --enable-camera \
  --use-csi \
  --stereo \
  --calibration tools/vision/calibration/output_960/stereo_calibration.npz \
  --baseline-override 52.5 \
  --port /dev/ttyACM0 \
  --device 0 \
  --disable-world-tracking
```

The belief controller keeps a yaw/pitch target belief in turret coordinates, smooths detections, estimates short-lived target velocity, coasts briefly through missed detections, rejects unconfirmed far jumps, and drives the servos in a separate control loop. The test tuning around this work used belief update alpha `0.75`, pitch alpha `0.35`, miss decay `0.90`, min confidence `0.15`, max age `1.0s`, jump distance `160` raw units with two matching detections, yaw/pitch velocity caps `600/180 raw/s`, and prediction up to `0.45s`. The UI's **Clear Belief** control resets belief and PID state without recentering the turret.

## Can/cup/bottle comparison test

This is the recovered raw-COCO comparison command, forced onto the belief controller:

```bash
cd ~/rat-inference
docker stop rat-inference 2>/dev/null || true
./run.sh rt200 \
  --model yolo11n.pt \
  --target-class bottle \
  --target-class cup \
  --confidence 0.30 \
  --device 0 \
  --disable-world-tracking
docker logs -f rat-inference
```

For the corresponding world-tracker comparison, omit `--disable-world-tracking`. The later final world-tracking command was shortened to:

```bash
./run.sh rt200 --model yolo11n.pt --confidence 0.30 --device 0
```

Note: the test can was only detected as COCO `cup` at about `0.06` confidence in one captured frame, so `0.30` can still produce no accepted boxes. For a can-only diagnostic, temporarily try `--confidence 0.05`, use a clearer COCO-style bottle/cup, or use the custom rat model for actual rat testing.

